# Growth Governance

Use this rule to keep long-term structure clean while the project grows.

## Decide the domain first

- If work targets `src/app/[locale]/...`, follow **sito madre** standards (i18n copy, SEO metadata, localized routes).
- If work targets `src/funnels/**` or `src/app/funnel-internal/**`, follow **funnel** standards (registry-driven routing, conversion tracking, no locale prefixes).
- Never mix page components between site and funnel areas.

## Mandatory references before implementing

- Read architecture rules in `.cursor/rules/site-architecture.mdc` and `.cursor/rules/funnel-architecture.mdc`.
- For SEO-sensitive site pages, apply `.cursor/rules/site-seo.mdc` and `.cursor/rules/release-checklist.mdc`.
- For funnels, apply tracking + config rules and keep behavior declarative in `src/funnels/registry.ts`.

## Anti-regression checks

- Prefer registry/config changes over slug hardcoding in page/layout files.
- Keep funnel component contract in a single source (`src/funnels/component-contract.ts`).
- When changing public assets or docs for release quality, follow:
  - `docs/public-asset-policy.md`
  - `docs/growth-governance.md`
  - `docs/funnel-and-page-checklist.md`

## Validation loop after substantive changes

- Run relevant checks before closure:
  - `npm run lint`
  - `npm run typecheck`
  - `npm run test`
  - `npm run check:public-assets`
  - `npm run report:health` for structural trend visibility
